# Never Commit to Main

- **Do not commit to the `main` branch.** Always work on a feature branch.
- Before staging or committing, check the current branch. If it is `main`, create and switch to a new branch first (e.g. `git checkout -b feature/your-feature`), then stage and commit.
- If the user asks to commit and you are on `main`, create a new branch from `main`, switch to it, then stage and commit there. Tell the user which branch was used.
